From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:53:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Wake on the Smart Cover

Make the D2207 GPIO node the PMU event controller, as on the iPad 5 and
6. The PMU event line is SoC GPIO 86: Apple's device tree gives
/arm-io/i2c0/pmu "interrupts" 0x56 with flags 1 and interrupt-parent
/arm-io/gpio, on both the J81 and the J82, and the same flags on the
iPad 6 are its active-low line.

List the two Smart Cover hall sensors, GPIO 12 ("halleffect") and 10
("halleffect1"), as wake-only events 0x24 and 0x22, so that opening the
cover ends system sleep. While awake they stay polled.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index 4deccfa..7cc35c4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -152,6 +152,11 @@
 			/* Only Bluetooth (2) and Wi-Fi (3) REG_ON are used; the other lines stay as iBoot left them. */
 			gpio-reserved-ranges = <0 2>, <4 6>, <11 1>, <13 8>;
 			/* Lines 10 and 12 are the Smart Cover hall sensors. */
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 86 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+			/* Smart Cover hall sensors (lines 10 and 12): wake only. */
+			apple,wake-events = <0x22 0x24>;
 		};
 
 		rtc@5c0 {
